C suite build and packaging

From c/, install prerequisites and build out of source:

  ./install-deps.sh
  make JOBS=4
  make test
  sudo make install

Debian/Ubuntu/Mint use apt; RHEL/Rocky/Alma/Fedora use dnf.
CMake 3.20+, a C compiler, make, Python 3, git, libaio, pciutils, NUMA,
readline and UUID development packages are required. The helper installs them.

Linux defaults to /usr/bin: spitc, fsfiller and the other C utilities.
Use PREFIX=/path only for an intentional custom install. Rust spit is separate
and installs as /usr/bin/spit; it does not use C spitchecker's data format.

  make dist         native DEB/RPM, with build/test checks
  make deb          Debian package using debhelper
  make rpm          RPM and source RPM using rpmbuild
  make source       source archive with offline version metadata

The Debian directory is debian/; the RPM spec is packaging/stutools-c.spec.
The package is stutools-c and can coexist with Rust stutools 2.0.

For direct CMake builds:

  cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build --parallel 4
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -L smoke
  sudo cmake --install build

In-source cmake builds are intentionally rejected. The built C target remains
build/spit/spit, while installation names it spitc. macOS/Windows build the
limited portable backend; the complete C suite requires Linux.

Write/discard workloads destroy data within their selected ranges. Use the
help and man pages and a disposable target before running storage tests.
